WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.281
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.581 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:16.308
Unit thirty-six: Time Clauses (when / while / before / after). Today you will say when things happen in relation to other events.

4
00:00:16.608 --> 00:00:19.318
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.372
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:24.869
When.

7
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:27.465
When means at the time that.

8
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.759
When I get home, I eat.

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.329
Your turn. Say: When.

10
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:35.947
When.

11
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:37.638
While.

12
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.313
While means during the time that.

13
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:42.916
I listen to music while I cook.

14
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:46.285
Your turn. Say: While.

15
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:49.983
While.

16
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.647
Before.

17
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.429
Before means earlier than.

18
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:56.761
Wash your hands before you eat.

19
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.700
Your turn. Say: Before.

20
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.440
Before.

21
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:05.045
After.

22
00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.632
After means later than.

23
00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:09.903
After class, we play.

24
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:12.647
Your turn. Say: After.

25
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.315
After.

26
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.295
As soon as.

27
00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:21.236
As soon as means immediately when.

28
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.617
Call me as soon as you arrive.

29
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.463
Your turn. Say: As soon as.

30
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.510
As soon as.

31
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.286
Until.

32
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:35.318
Until means up to the time that.

33
00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:37.429
Wait until I come.

34
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:40.228
Your turn. Say: Until.

35
00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.010
Until.

36
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.099
Time clause.

37
00:01:47.083 --> 00:01:50.151
Time clause means a clause that says when something happens.

38
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.819
A time clause begins with when.

39
00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:56.243
Your turn. Say: Time clause.

40
00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.298
Time clause.

41
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.132
Present simple.

42
00:02:03.117 --> 00:02:06.742
Present simple means the tense used in future time clauses.

43
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.617
Use the present simple after when.

44
00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:13.275
Your turn. Say: Present simple.

45
00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.239
Present simple.

46
00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:21.545
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:24.406
Visal, what do you do when you get home?

48
00:02:25.517 --> 00:02:35.625
When I get home, I do my homework. A time clause tells us when something happens. It starts with when, while, before, after, as soon as or until.

49
00:02:36.717 --> 00:02:38.995
What tense do we use for the future?

50
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:51.167
We use the present simple, not will, in the time clause: When I arrive, I will call you. Not when I will arrive. The main clause can use will.

51
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:54.492
What is the difference between when and while?

52
00:02:55.583 --> 00:03:09.375
When is for a point in time or a short action. While is for a long action: I listen to music while I cook. Before and after show order. Until means up to the moment.

53
00:03:10.533 --> 00:03:11.999
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:18.100
Grammar focus: Time clauses: when and while and before and after plus present simple.

55
00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.622
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.317 --> 00:03:22.084
When I get home, I do my homework.

57
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:25.285
Before we eat, we wash our hands.

58
00:03:26.183 --> 00:03:28.659
As soon as I arrive, I will call you.

59
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:38.684
Time clauses begin with when, while, before, after, as soon as or until. For the future, use the present simple in the time clause, and will in the main clause.

60
00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.799
Be careful! Don't say: When I will arrive, I call you.

61
00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:47.035
Say: When I arrive, I will call you.

62
00:03:47.335 --> 00:03:49.427
Use present simple after when.

63
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:52.804
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.857
Before and After.

65
00:03:55.157 --> 00:03:57.110
When I get home, I do my homework.

66
00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.216
I listen to music while I cook dinner.

67
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.699
Before we eat, we wash our hands.

68
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.605
After the class finishes, we play football.

69
00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.785
As soon as I arrive, I will call you.

70
00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.053
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:18.951
When I blank home, I will call you.

72
00:04:19.251 --> 00:04:23.079
A, will arrive. B, arrive. C, arrived.

73
00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.424
The answer is B: arrive.

74
00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:31.653
Wash your hands blank you eat.

75
00:04:31.953 --> 00:04:35.304
A, before. B, after. C, until.

76
00:04:38.867 --> 00:04:40.947
The answer is A: before.

77
00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:45.490
I read blank I wait for the bus. (long action)

78
00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:49.200
A, while. B, after. C, until.

79
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:54.814
The answer is A: while.

80
00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.601
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.901 --> 00:05:04.179
A, When I will go, I call you.. B, When I go, I will call you.. C, When I go, I will to call you..

82
00:05:07.733 --> 00:05:10.313
The answer is B: When I go, I will call you..

83
00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.576
According to the reading, what do they do before they eat?

84
00:05:14.876 --> 00:05:19.307
A, wash their hands. B, play football. C, call a friend.

85
00:05:22.867 --> 00:05:25.307
The answer is A: wash their hands.

86
00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.547
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:30.383 --> 00:05:32.696
Write two sentences with 'when' or 'before'.

88
00:05:41.483 --> 00:05:42.995
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:43.295 --> 00:05:54.762
When I wake up, I brush my teeth. Before I go to school, I eat breakfast. In both sentences I use the present simple in the time clause because I talk about my routine.

90
00:05:55.062 --> 00:05:56.725
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:57.617 --> 00:06:04.634
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and time clauses: when and while and before and after plus present simple.

92
00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:09.166
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

93
00:06:09.466 --> 00:06:12.222
See you in Unit thirty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:12.522 --> 00:06:14.768
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

